+cowrie.policy.decision
+======================
+
+MIRAGE: the policy gate decided how to answer a simple command (only emitted
+when ``[mirage] policy_enabled`` is true).
+
+Attributes:
+
+    * `input`: the expanded command line
+    * `action`: ``allow``, ``delay``, ``fake_success``, ``fake_error`` or ``terminate``
+    * `fallback`: true when no valid decision arrived in time and ``allow`` was used
+    * `known`: whether the emulated shell implements the command
+    * `decision_id`: the policy service's identifier for the decision
+    * `propensity`: probability the policy gave the chosen action
+    * `latency_ms`: time spent waiting for the decision
+    * `request_id`: identifier of the request sent to the policy service
+
